From: Bert Belder <bertbelder@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Index wasm code ranges under an embedder shared-allocation scope

The wasm code manager is a process-wide singleton, held by the
process-wide GlobalWasmState, and its lookup_map_ indexes every code
space region of every NativeModule in the process by address. The map
grows from whichever isolate compiled the module a region belongs to,
and every isolate reads it: LookupCode() resolves a program counter to
its WasmCode for a trap, for stack iteration and for the deoptimizer, so
a turn of any isolate descends a tree whose nodes the isolates that
compiled before it placed.

An embedder that gives each isolate its own allocation arena,
unaddressable from every other isolate, then finds those nodes in the
arena of whichever isolate grew the map, where the next isolate's
LookupCode faults.

Let such an embedder define a pair of weak hook functions, under which
the two insertions into the map run, so that it can switch the calling
thread's allocation onto memory every isolate shares for the duration.
Erasing a range needs no scope: it frees a node and rebalances the tree,
which writes only nodes the insertions placed. Without the hooks nothing
changes.
---
diff --git a/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc b/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
--- a/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
+++ b/src/wasm/wasm-code-manager.cc
@@ -68,6 +68,27 @@
 #include "src/heap/code-range.h"
 #include "src/init/isolate-group.h"
 #endif  // V8_OS_IOS
+
+// The process-wide wasm code manager and the embedder's allocator. The code
+// manager's {lookup_map_} indexes every code space region of every
+// NativeModule in the process by address, and it grows from whichever isolate
+// compiled the module a region belongs to. Every isolate reads it: LookupCode()
+// resolves a program counter to its WasmCode for a trap, for stack iteration
+// and for the deoptimizer. An embedder that gives each isolate its own
+// allocation arena, unaddressable from other isolates, needs those nodes placed
+// elsewhere: it defines the two functions below (both or neither), and the
+// insertions into the map then run between an enter and the matching leave, so
+// that the nodes go where the embedder puts memory shared by every isolate. The
+// token the enter returns is handed back to the leave.
+#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)
+extern "C" {
+uintptr_t v8_wasm_code_manager_shared_allocation_enter() __attribute__((weak));
+void v8_wasm_code_manager_shared_allocation_leave(uintptr_t token)
+    __attribute__((weak));
+}
+#define V8_HAS_WASM_CODE_MANAGER_SHARED_ALLOCATION_HOOKS 1
+#endif
+
 #define TRACE_HEAP(...)                                       \
   do {                                                        \
     if (v8_flags.trace_wasm_native_heap) PrintF(__VA_ARGS__); \
@@ -2320,8 +2341,40 @@
 #endif  // V8_OS_IOS
 }
 
+namespace {
+// Enters the embedder's shared-allocation state for the lifetime of the scope,
+// when the embedder provides it (see the hooks above).
+class CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope final {
+ public:
+  CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope() {
+#ifdef V8_HAS_WASM_CODE_MANAGER_SHARED_ALLOCATION_HOOKS
+    if (v8_wasm_code_manager_shared_allocation_enter != nullptr) {
+      token_ = v8_wasm_code_manager_shared_allocation_enter();
+      active_ = true;
+    }
+#endif
+  }
+  ~CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope() {
+#ifdef V8_HAS_WASM_CODE_MANAGER_SHARED_ALLOCATION_HOOKS
+    if (active_) v8_wasm_code_manager_shared_allocation_leave(token_);
+#endif
+  }
+  CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope(const CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope&) =
+      delete;
+  CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope& operator=(
+      const CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope&) = delete;
+
+ private:
+  uintptr_t token_ = 0;
+  bool active_ = false;
+};
+}  // namespace
+
 void WasmCodeManager::AssignRange(base::AddressRegion region,
                                   NativeModule* native_module) {
+  // The node this inserts belongs to the process and not to the calling
+  // isolate, which is the one that happens to have compiled {native_module}.
+  CodeManagerSharedAllocationScope shared_allocation;
   base::MutexGuard lock(&native_modules_mutex_);
   lookup_map_.insert(std::make_pair(
       region.begin(), std::make_pair(region.end(), native_module)));
